T2  - 2013 INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON SIGNAL-IMAGE TECHNOLOGY & INTERNET-BASED SYSTEMS (SITIS)
CP  - 9th International Conference on Signal-Image Technology and Internet-Based Systems (SITIS)
AB  - Process Management software and solutions mainly address structured processes in enterprises, but there are still many business applications that are less structured by their nature, such as human-centric and ad hoc workflows. Existing process mining algorithms often have difficulties in extracting a skeletal structure of a less-structured process model from real-life event logs. We propose a new process mining algorithm by using a skeleton-extraction procedure, which brings structure to less structured business processes. We present experimental mining results from real insurance claim examination event logs and verified the effectiveness of the proposed algorithm
