AB  - Safety-critical systems in domains such as aviation, railway, and automotive are often subject to a formal process of safety certification. The goal of this process is to ensure that these systems will operate safely without posing risks to the user, the public, or the environment [1]. It is typically expensive and time consuming for companies to certify their software. Therefore, any attempt to automate any part of the required process is very appreciated. In this research project, we report on our on-going project with an industry partner in the avionics domain, where we propose a framework to combine specification mining, model-based testing, and analytics to help with monitoring and verification of safety critical systems.
